    "note": "Third reader: as passed by its first chamber (Senate); title and scope were changed by amendment from gun buyback only to 'Firearm Safety and Firearm Crimes'. Struck by amendment: 'PERSON OR ENTITY' as operator of buyback programs (now federal firearms licensee or law enforcement agency) and 'TRADED IN' (now surrendered). Also added by amendment: 6-month deadline for destruction (§ 5-902(B)(1)(II)1), exemption for firearms found stolen or evidence of a crime (§ 5-902(A)), and a no-exception-to-other-law clause (§ 5-902(E)). Senate third-reading passage vote 45-0 (March 15, 2024); amendments made after the version read are not in the text read. § 5-140(b) is quoted as shown, with 'FELONY' replacing 'misdemeanor'; the plain text of § 5-140 (a), (c) is printed as part of the amendment."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 4-111(b)): (12) AN EMPLOYEE OF THE DEPARTMENT OF NATURAL RESOURCES IN THE COURSE OF PERFORMING OFFICIAL DUTIES.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 7-104(g)): (1) THIS SUBSECTION DOES NOT APPLY TO THEFT OF A FIREARM, AS DEFINED IN § 5–101 OF THE PUBLIC SAFETY ARTICLE.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Criminal Law § 7-104(H)): (H) A PERSON CONVICTED OF THEFT OF A FIREARM, AS DEFINED IN § 5–101 OF THE PUBLIC SAFETY ARTICLE, IS GUILTY OF A FELONY AND IS SUBJECT TO IMPRISONMENT NOT EXCEEDING 5 YEARS OR A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $1,000 OR BOTH.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-140): (b) A person who violates this section is guilty of a FELONY and on conviction is subject to imprisonment not exceeding 10 years or a fine not exceeding $25,000 or both.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-902): (B) (1) (I) SUBJECT TO SUBPARAGRAPH (II) OF THIS PARAGRAPH, A FEDERAL FIREARMS LICENSEE OR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY OPERATING A GUN BUYBACK PROGRAM SHALL DESTROY EACH FIREARM, INCLUDING EVERY COMPONENT AND PART ATTACHED TO THE FIREARM, THAT IS SURRENDERED TO THE FEDERAL FIREARMS LICENSEE OR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY AT A GUN BUYBACK PROGRAM.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-902): (C) A FEDERAL FIREARMS LICENSEE OR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCY THAT VIOLATES THIS SECTION IS SUBJECT TO A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $10,000 PER VIOLATION.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-114(b)): (XI) VIOLATES SUBTITLE 9 OF THIS TITLE."
}